BOT d1 18:30 SAY     Dusk. A dark carpet comes down over the square.
BOT d1 18:30 PLACE   weaver, Anarvan
BOT d1 18:30 BEAT    prologue: arrival
BOT d1 18:30 STORY   Farrokh lights the oil lamp with a word - "a weaver's sleight of hand", he smiles
BOT d1 18:30 STORY   Dusk. A dark carpet comes down over the square.
BOT d1 18:30 STATUS  on foot, hp 100, food 73, water 72, rest 78, weaver, Anarvan, story: arrival
BOT d1 18:30 SAY     Farrokh: They say... Sekheho builds an observatory, they say.
BOT d1 18:30 SAY     Farrokh: If you are going to Shotnagar, it is 1 days' ride to the east.
BOT d1 18:30 SAY     Farrokh: In the old days... In the year 1089 the faithless men of Sohtashta rose against us over revenge. At the Weeping Bridge the armies of Dhaadhrashta won a glorious victory; their dead lay in thousands.
BOT d1 18:31 SAY     Farrokh: As for the gods... Magic is a sacred gift to us.
BOT d1 18:31 SAY     The door opens
BOT d1 18:31 SAY     The door closes
BOT d1 18:32 STORY   Azhdar: "Give me the Weave!" No one understands him.
BOT d1 18:42 SAY     Farrokh presses a plain rug and a small bag into your arms: "Hide. Don't come out, whatever you hear."
BOT d1 18:42 BEAT    prologue: handover
BOT d1 18:42 STORY   Farrokh presses a plain rug and a small bag into your arms: "Hide. Don't come out, whatever you hear."
BOT d1 18:42 DO      runs to hide in the cellar
BOT d1 18:42 DO      walks to Farrokh's door
BOT d1 18:43 SAY     The door opens
BOT d1 18:43 SAY     The door closes
BOT d1 19:01 SAY     Codex: Dead tree observed
BOT d1 19:11 SAY     The hatch closes over you. The cellar is warded.
BOT d1 19:12 BEAT    prologue: hiding
BOT d1 19:12 STORY   The hatch closes over you. The cellar is warded.
BOT d1 19:12 STORY   Fire roars over the roofs.
BOT d1 19:22 STORY   Screams in the street.
BOT d1 19:33 STORY   Farrokh's magic flares, blue and bright, and is gone.
BOT d1 19:44 STORY   Azhdar burns carpet after carpet: "Where is it?"
BOT d1 19:55 STORY   "It is near. I feel it near." Then hoofbeats, and silence.
